    "title": "What channel is NY Mets vs Dodgers today? How to watch, prediction",
    "text": "April 13, 2026, 3:52 p.m. ETThe New York Mets look to get back in the win column as they get ready face off against the Los Angeles Dodgers on Monday night at Dodger Stadium.The Mets (7-9, last in NL East), similar to the Yankees, come into the week on a five-game losing streak after getting swept by the Athletics at home over the weekend.You have to go back to last Tuesday, April 7, to find the Mets last win which came in the series opener versus the Diamondbacks in extra innings.Then you have the Dodgers (11-4, first in NL West), the reigning, back-to-back World Series champions who are an MLB-best winning 11 of their first 15 games and have won four of their first five series in their quest for a three-peat, most recently taking two of three games versus the Texas Rangers.Here's what you need to know on how to watch, the starting pitchers and our prediction for tonight's series opener between the Mets and Dodgers in L.A.:What time is NY Mets vs Dodgers game today?Time: 10:10 p.m.What channel is NY Mets vs Dodgers today?TV: SNYHow to stream NY Mets vs Dodgers game todayStreaming: MLB.TV for out of market viewersNY Mets, Dodgers starting pitchers todayMets: David Peterson (0-2, 6.14 ERA)Dodgers: Justin Wrobleski (1-0, 4.00 ERA)It was another rough outing for Peterson his last time out. After giving up five runs on nine hits with two walks in 4 1/3 innings in a 7-2 loss against the San Francisco Giants on April 2, the 30-year-old southpaw's following start had nearly identical numbers: five runs allowed, six hits given up and two walks in a 7-2 loss to the Arizona Diamondbacks on April 8. This is the polar opposite of how Peterson performed in his 2026 debut when he threw 5 1/3 shutout innings versus the Pittsburgh Pirates on March 28.Wrobleski earned his first win of the season in his last start. He went five innings and conceded just one run on two hits in the Dodgers' 14-2 victory on April 6. While being a short sample size, the 25-year-old lefty does have more walks (five) than strikeouts (four) in nine innings of work so far in 2026.NY Mets vs Dodgers odds for today's gameOdds according to BetMGM as of Monday, April 13:Spread: Dodgers by 1.5Over/under: 8.5Moneyline: Dodgers (-170), Mets (+140)Prediction for Mets vs Dodgers todayDavid Peterson's early season struggles continue at Dodger Stadium on Monday night, as the Mets offense isn't able to keep up with the Dodgers offensive firepower in the series opener.Dodgers 7, Mets 4",
